<title>UK: BANK OF IRELAND UPS STRUCTURED FRN TO $175 MILLION.</title>
<headline>BANK OF IRELAND UPS STRUCTURED FRN TO $175 MILLION.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following structured floating rate issue has been increased to $175 million from $150 million, joint lead managers J.P. Morgan and Salomon Brothers said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The deal was launched on Tuesday.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BANK OF IRELAND</p>
<p> AMT	  $175 MLN  BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY	*SEP.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN    *+25 BP    PAY DATE    04.SEP.97</p>
<p> LAST MOODY A2	  ISS PRICE  99.945    FULL FEES   0.40</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P   A-	  REOFFER    99.945</p>
<p> LISTING    LONDON    DENOMS (K) 10	  SALE LIMITS US/GB/IE</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 1</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  IRELAND   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.20	SELL CONC  0.20	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> NOTES    **CALL AT PAR AFTER FIVE YEARS AFTER WHICH THE MARGIN</p>
<p>		STEPS UP TO 75 BP. ISSUED OFF EMTN PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
